    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all 38 tests pass, including the 2 new `Cp27Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `GET /api/owners/{id}` to return `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`. Following the existing `membershipLevel` pattern in this codebase, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient` computed getter:\n   ```java\n   public String getContactPreference() {\n       return (this.email != null && !this.email.isBlank()) ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` property (enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct's `toOwnerDto` maps it automatically by name.\n\nNo wiring or new function classes were needed since the response DTO is built by the existing `RespondWithOwner` step via the mapper.",
